id: blockade
name: Blockade
type: counter
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerTier: 2
attacking: false
blockade: true
resource: blockaded
resourceMax: 1
resourceLabel: Blockaded
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Cut somebody off mid-Movement. A Clash of Impulsive against theirs; win and they
  stop where they are, get their Actions and Ki back, and cannot use the Movement
  Maneuver again this turn.
text: >
  Blockade Maneuver: Protect your allies by standing in the way.
  –Maneuver Type: Counter
  –Action Cost: 1 Counter
  –KP Cost: 2(T)
  –Effect: If a Character within range of your Normal Speed uses the Movement
  Maneuver, you may use this Maneuver to make a Clash (Impulsive) against that
  Character. If you win, you may immediately move to any Square within your Normal
  Speed that is adjacent to that Character. That Character stops using the Movement
  Maneuver and cannot use the Movement Maneuver for the remainder of their Turn
  (they regain any Actions or Ki Points spent). If you lose, that Character may
  continue to use their Movement Maneuver and you trigger their Exploit Maneuver.

---

# No script here, and one belonging to somebody else.
#
# `blockade: true` hands this to the code, for the reason every Counter Maneuver
# that does more than pay for itself is handed there: it is played from the card of
# the Maneuver it answers, and a script cannot reach one.
#
# What it comes to:
#   - offered on a Movement Maneuver's card, to anybody but the Character moving
#   - a Clash of Impulsive against Impulsive - one Saving Throw named, so there is
#     nothing to choose and nobody is asked
#   - winning says how far you may step to reach them, stops the Movement, hands
#     back the Actions and the Ki it cost, and leaves them Blockaded
#   - losing provokes their Exploit Maneuver against you, and their Movement goes on
#
# --- The Resource, and whose file its rule is in ------------------------------------
#
# "Cannot use the Movement Maneuver for the remainder of their Turn." That is a
# forbid, and a forbid has to be written by a passive on the Character it binds - so
# it cannot be here: a Trait's passives run on whoever owns it, and the Character
# being blocked does not own this Maneuver.
#
# What they do own is the Movement Maneuver itself, which every character carries a
# copy of. So the Resource is declared here, where the rule that hands it out lives,
# and read by a passive in maneuvers/movement.dbu, which is the only file that runs
# on the right person. That file says the same thing pointing this way.
#
# It is a Resource rather than a Combat Condition because there is no published
# Condition for this and inventing one would be inventing rules. A Resource is the
# system's own bookkeeping, it takes a clock of its own - the end of their turn - and
# it shows on their sheet beside the other counters, so the player can see what is
# stopping them and when it lifts.
#
# --- What is not built, and why -----------------------------------------------------
#
# "A Character within range of your Normal Speed", and "any Square within your Normal
# Speed that is adjacent to that Character". Both are facts about the map, and this
# system moves nobody: the card says how many Squares your Normal Speed is and the
# token is yours to drag. Whether they were in range at all is the table's call, the
# same as every other range in these rules.
